   <chapter title="Overview">
       <p><b>File:</b> <code>OtherTests/IndividualClientFunctionality/Add_Edit_Delete_Client_Action_test.cy.ts</code></p>
        <p><b>Folder:</b> <code>OtherTests/IndividualClientFunctionality</code></p>
        <p><b>Description:</b> Validates end-to-end CRUD for client Actions, including creating required Settings (Action Category, Action Status), then Add, Edit, and Delete on an individual client</p>
        <p><b>Priority:</b> High</p>
        <p><b>Owner:</b> QA Team</p>
        <p><b>Tags:</b> regression, actions, tasks, individual</p>
        <p><b>Dependencies:</b> faker-js, navigateToNewestClientMenu</p>
    </chapter>

    <chapter title="Test Suites">
        <chapter title="Add, Edit, Delete Client Action (Task)">
        </chapter>
    </chapter>

    <chapter title="Test Scenarios">
        <procedure title="Add Client Action" id="test-1">
            <p>Ensures an Action Category and an Action Status exist so they can be selected during client action creation</p>
            <step>Open Settings → Actions Setup</step>
            <step>Add Action Category “Action Category Test” with random mapping ref and save</step>
            <step>Navigate to Action Statuses and add “Action Status Test” with random mapping ref and save</step>
            <chapter title="Expected Results">
                <p>• Action Category and Action Status records are available in dropdowns on the client Actions form</p>
            </chapter>
        </procedure>
        <procedure title="Edit Action" id="test-2">
            <p>Ensures an Action Category and an Action Status exist so they can be selected during client action creation</p>
            <step>Open Settings → Actions Setup</step>
            <step>Add Action Category “Action Category Test” with random mapping ref and save</step>
            <step>Navigate to Action Statuses and add “Action Status Test” with random mapping ref and save</step>
            <chapter title="Expected Results">
                <p>• Action Category and Action Status records are available in dropdowns on the client Actions form</p>
            </chapter>
        </procedure>
        <procedure title="Delete Action" id="test-3">
            <p>Ensures an Action Category and an Action Status exist so they can be selected during client action creation</p>
            <step>Open Settings → Actions Setup</step>
            <step>Add Action Category “Action Category Test” with random mapping ref and save</step>
            <step>Navigate to Action Statuses and add “Action Status Test” with random mapping ref and save</step>
            <chapter title="Expected Results">
